===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|sign}}
From {{der|en|enm|mark}}, {{m|enm|merk}}, {{m|enm|merke}}, from {{der|en|ang|mearc||mark, sign, line of division; standard; boundary, limit, term, border; defined area, district, province}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*marku}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*markō||boundary; boundary marker}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mórǵs||edge, boundary, border}}.

Compare {{m|en|march}}.
