##* {{quote-song|sv|year=1996|author={{w|Drängarna}} [The Farmhands]|album=w:sv:Fint vettö|trans-album=Nice Y'know|title=Kung över ängarna|trans-title=King of [over] the Meadows|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UlcFueNNpMY|text=Jag lägger mig i gräset ner. Ligger still och bara {{l|sv|ler}}. {{l|sv|slumrar|Slumrar}} {{l|sv|till|id=sudden and brief}} och {{l|sv|snarkar}} tyst. Drömmer om en kvinnas {{l|sv|byst}}. Då ser jag nån som emot mig går, {{l|sv|liderlig}} med {{l|sv|utsläppt}} hår. Hon är {{l|sv|vacker som en dag}}. I samma stund {{l|sv|så|id=adverbial filler}} {{l|sv|vaknar}} jag. {{l|sv|svär|Svär}} [bit hard to make out the S] ett {{l|sv|tag}} men tänker sen: Hon kommer nog till mig inatt igen. {{l|sv|ännu|Ännu}} lyser solen stark i skog och '''mark'''.|t=I lie down in the grass {{q-q|"{{lang|sv|Jag lägger mig ner i gräset}}" is the usual word order. {{m|sv|ner|Ner|down}} can be skipped}}. [I] lie still and just grin [or smile]. [I] doze off and snore quietly. [I] dream of a woman's bosom. Then I see someone walking towards me {{q-q|"{{lang|sv|Då ser jag nån som går emot mig}}" is the usual word order}}, lustful {{q-q|in an unrestrained manner – old-fashioned – often used to imply "lecherous," but also more generally}} with her hair let down {{q-q|with out-released hair}}. She is pretty as a picture {{q-q|"beautiful as a day" – idiom}}. At that moment {{q-q|in the same moment}} I wake up. [I] swear for a bit but then [I] think: She will probably come to me tonight again {{q-q|"{{lang|sv|Igen inatt}}" is a more common word order in Swedish as well}}. The sun still shines bright {{q-q|"yet shines (V2 word order) the sun strong" – could be translated as "still the sun shines bright" to match, but sounds less awkward in Swedish}} in woods and fields {{q-q|"forest and '''land'''" – idiomatic}}. {{q-q|Could also be put in the present continuous. Matches the intuition in Swedish with the [I]s. See the usage notes for {{m|sv|-r}}.}}}}
